{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589275295,"sessionID":"ses_e2a2563d8ffeBnCNuk46hsD3mF","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5db3174001HGyUeFVfloL5Vj","sessionID":"ses_e2a2563d8ffeBnCNuk46hsD3mF","messageID":"msg_1d5daf872001uHofmbNTd82WLg","type":"tool","id":"call_4b6bcdf7dd154c338bf4f6af","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"awk '/^- \\[ \\] T010 /{print; exit}' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"- [ ] T010 [P] Run no code from an untrusted backfill checkout (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('runs nothing from a checkout that is neither the project root nor a marked arena')`: make a temporary folder holding a fake `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` and a fake `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, each writing its own marker file into that folder when run, write a one-line log whose `locator.projectDir` names the folder, call `backfillRunLog` with `promptFor: () => 'prompt'`, `brief: async () => 'unknown'` and the default warm and replay, and expect `ok` true, `lines` 1, `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` on the written line and neither marker file. Add `it('replays a checkout that holds the arena marker')`, where the folder also holds `.git/skilled-behaviour-arena` and stub `warm` and `replay` record their `checkoutDir`, expecting both to record that folder. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the first case fail because both fakes ran. Then in `CO` add `realpathSync` to the `node:fs` import and `export function trustedCheckout(checkoutDir)`, which returns `true` when `realpathSync(checkoutDir)` equals `realpathSync(REPO_ROOT)` or `existsSync(join(checkoutDir, '.git', 'skilled-behaviour-arena'))` holds, and `false` when either call throws, with a comment that a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Give `backfillRunLog` a `trusted = trustedCheckout` option, named in its jsdoc, and before the warm-up, when `checkoutDir !== null && !trusted(checkoutDir)`, set the offer to `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'untrusted_checkout' }` and skip the warm-up and the replay. In the existing case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once`, pass `trusted: () => true`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-backfill-trust.mjs` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false` and `offerError: \"untrusted_checkout\"`.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T010 [P] Run no code from an untrusted backfill checkout (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('runs nothing from a checkout that is neither the project root nor a marked arena')`: make a temporary folder holding a fake `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` and a fake `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, each writing its own marker file into that folder when run, write a one-line log whose `locator.projectDir` names the folder, call `backfillRunLog` with `promptFor: () => 'prompt'`, `brief: async () => 'unknown'` and the default warm and replay, and expect `ok` true, `lines` 1, `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` on the written line and neither marker file. Add `it('replays a checkout that holds the arena marker')`, where the folder also holds `.git/skilled-behaviour-arena` and stub `warm` and `replay` record their `checkoutDir`, expecting both to record that folder. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the first case fail because both fakes ran. Then in `CO` add `realpathSync` to the `node:fs` import and `export function trustedCheckout(checkoutDir)`, which returns `true` when `realpathSync(checkoutDir)` equals `realpathSync(REPO_ROOT)` or `existsSync(join(checkoutDir, '.git', 'skilled-behaviour-arena'))` holds, and `false` when either call throws, with a comment that a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Give `backfillRunLog` a `trusted = trustedCheckout` option, named in its jsdoc, and before the warm-up, when `checkoutDir !== null && !trusted(checkoutDir)`, set the offer to `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'untrusted_checkout' }` and skip the warm-up and the replay. In the existing case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout once`, pass `trusted: () => true`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node $PL/probe-backfill-trust.mjs` prints `fake CLI ran: false, fake hook ran: false` and `offerError: \"untrusted_checkout\"`.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"awk '/^- \\\\[ \\\\] T010 /{print; exit}' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589274484,"end":1794589275295}}}}
